---
# Per-API-key rate limit for the API Product, written as a plain
# RateLimitPolicy (not a PlanPolicy).
#
# === Two upstream gaps we work around here ===
#
# (1) #2047 — PlanPolicy emits one shared Limitador counter PER TIER, so
#     every subscriber on the same plan competes for the same bucket. To
#     give each subscriber an independent quota we have to write the RLP
#     by hand and add `counters: [request.headers['x-consumer-id']]`.
#     https://github.com/Kuadrant/kuadrant-operator/issues/2047
#
# (2) WASM rate-limit `when:` predicates see neither `auth.identity`
#     (resolves to null — UnsupportedIndex) nor authorino-injected
#     request headers (NoSuchKey on x-plan-id, x-consumer-id etc). So we
#     can't gate distinct rates per tier from inside this RLP — only the
#     COUNTER expression can read the injected header, not the predicate.
#     Result: ONE bucket size for everyone, scoped per consumer.
#
# Effect for the lab: every API key gets its own quota — the gold/silver/
# bronze tier distinction is COSMETIC at this layer (the dev portal still
# labels keys per tier; the gateway throttles them all at the same rate).
# The first {limit, window} from `apps_connectivity_plans` is used for
# everyone; explicit `unlimited: true` tiers are skipped when picking it.
# Switch back to a PlanPolicy once both gaps land upstream.
apiVersion: kuadrant.io/v1
kind: RateLimitPolicy
metadata:
  name: {{ apps_connectivity_planpolicy_name }}
  namespace: {{ apps_namespace }}
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: rhcl-banking-poc
    rhcl.redhat.com/replaces: PlanPolicy
    rhcl.redhat.com/upstream-issue: kuadrant-operator-2047
spec:
{% set rated = (apps_connectivity_plans | rejectattr('unlimited', 'defined') | list) + (apps_connectivity_plans | selectattr('unlimited', 'defined') | rejectattr('unlimited') | list) %}
{% set chosen = rated[0] if rated else apps_connectivity_plans[0] %}
  targetRef:
    group: gateway.networking.k8s.io
    kind: HTTPRoute
    name: {{ apps_connectivity_route_name }}
  limits:
    per-consumer:
      when:
        # `has(auth.identity)` is the safe form — `auth.identity` itself
        # would null-deref. Empty placeholder is treated as "no identity"
        # so anonymous requests (e.g. health probes) bypass the limit.
        - predicate: has(auth.identity)
      rates:
        - limit: {{ chosen.limit }}
          window: {{ chosen.window | string | to_json }}
      counters:
        # The AuthPolicy injects `x-consumer-id` as the Secret name. Single
        # quotes inside the bracket key because double quotes mid-CEL leak
        # through the operator's stringification and Limitador's YAML
        # parser rejects nested-double-quote forms.
        - expression: request.headers['x-consumer-id']
